title: Implement multi-origin batches
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    This PR adds an extension pallet `pallet-utility-ext` to `pallet-utility` which allows for
    batching calls with different origins in a single signed transaction. The origins can be
    custom, they don't have to be `RawOrigin::Signed(AccountId)`. This is done by supplying a
    number of batch items consisting of a call, its wrapping inner `TransactionExtension` and the
    origin the call is expected to run with, along with the submitter's nonce, to
    `pallet_utility_ext::batch_multi_origin` or `force_batch_multi_origin`. The multi origin
    batches behave like `batch` and `force_batch` respectively.

    Each item runs its inner pipeline in full before the next item starts, as if it were a
    transaction of its own included right after the previous item. Items are signed over an
    `ItemImplication` binding them to the batch, so they cannot be applied anywhere else. Items
    are not validated in the transaction pool, only the submitter's transaction is. The submitter
    pays for the whole batch up front like for any transaction, each item then pays for itself
    through its inner pipeline and the pallet's `MultiOriginBatch` extension, wrapping the
    runtime's fee payment extension, refunds the submitter the weight and bytes of every item
    whose pipeline ran to completion.

    Enabling this feature means configuring `pallet-utility-ext` in your runtime. Importantly, the
    pallet requires:

    - A maximum number of calls allowed in a single batch. This should generally be a low figure
      (e.g. 8 calls).
    - A call filter for which calls are allowed to be part of multi origin batches.
    - The inner `TransactionExtension` type which will wrap each of the calls inside the batch.
      This is meant to be a subset of the runtime's overarching `TransactionExtension`, with the
      one verifying signatures first and the fee payment extension included, but without the
      extensions which are supposed to run only once per transaction (e.g. `CheckWeight`,
      `WeightReclaim`).
    - A `FeeCredit` which sets the submitter's withdrawn fee aside while the items run,
      `pallet_transaction_payment::Pallet` for the fee payment extensions built on it.
    - The pallet's `MultiOriginBatch` extension wrapping the runtime's fee payment extension in
      its slot of the overarching `TransactionExtension`.

    `TransactionValidityError` and its variants now derive `DecodeWithMemTracking` in
    `sp-runtime`.
crates:
- name: pallet-utility-ext
  bump: major
- name: sp-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-sdk
  bump: minor
